 ## What is not here yet
 
-<!-- TODO: the two questions this format leaves open — who decides how many records one segment
-holds, and what happens when two segments hold the same series — and the steps that own them. Name
-`lakelet/4.8-compaction` and the reader promise it has to keep. -->
+Who decides how many records a segment holds, and what happens when two segments hold the same
+series, are open questions. `lakelet/4.8-compaction` owns both: it rewrites segments while readers
+keep reading, and its promise is that a query started before a merge and finished after it answers
+exactly what one that ran entirely before the merge would have. Nothing in this format prevents that
+— a segment is immutable, closed and self-describing — but nothing here decides when one ends
+either.
